,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamHaskell","html_url":"https://github.com/SamHaskell","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamHaskell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamHaskell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamHaskell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamHaskell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamHaskell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamHaskell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamHaskell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamHaskell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamHaskell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-09T17:52:00Z","updated_at":"2025-11-09T17:52:49Z","body":"I also noticed slightly slower latency in editor (similar to what @Atenvardo describes) and odd stuttering/poor frame pacing during play on tahoe 26.0.1. I tried pulling old stable versions back to Godot 4.2 and all of them had the same issues.\n\nI just grabbed tahoe 26.1 and while there definitely still feels like theres slightly increased latency in editor on general actions (clicking around, text input etc), the stuttering issues during play seem to be resolved. \n\nWith the latency, I could well just be misremembering how fluid the editor was beforehand, and have no machine to go back and check against as a reference as my macbook is my only option at the moment.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3508566217/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4363893281","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110600#issuecomment-4363893281","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110600","id":4363893281,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBBu6IQ","user":{"login":"Wobling","id":15089188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDg5MTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15089188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wobling","html_url":"https://github.com/Wobling","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wobling/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wobling/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wobling/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wobling/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wobling/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wobling/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wobling/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wobling/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wobling/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-02T13:33:19Z","updated_at":"2026-05-02T13:33:19Z","body":"> Are either of you using Magnet? See other open issues where it's mentioned: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues?q=sort%3Aupdated-desc%20is%3Aissue%20is%3Aopen%20magnet%20macos\n\nI have been having problems with the game Outhold which is built with Godot, I come looking for a potential solution to a massive delay between input and response. I closed Magnet and the delay is gone so there is absolutely some issues with Magnet and Godot.\n\nThanks for the suggestion.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4363893281/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5435116806","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110600#issuecomment-5435116806","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110600","id":5435116806,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ_VNBg","user":{"login":"V-outsider","id":70209157,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjA5MTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70209157?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/V-outsider","html_url":"https://github.com/V-outsider","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/V-outsider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/V-outsider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/V-outsider/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/V-outsider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/V-outsider/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/V-outsider/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/V-outsider/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/V-outsider/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/V-outsider/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T06:14:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T06:27:19Z","body":"Device: MacBook Pro M4 (Tahoe 26.5.2)\n\nI'm not sure if I'm in the right thread discussing the issue, but I'm currently experiencing a possibly similar problem. I wanted to create a custom cursor for the 2D game, using a scene with a custom sprite and a script:\n\n```\nextends Node2D\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n    Input.set_mouse_mode(Input.MOUSE_MODE_HIDDEN)\n    top_level = true\n\nfunc _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n    if event is InputEventMouseMotion:\n    global_position = event.position\n```\n\nThe funny thing is, when running in minimized windowed mode, everything is fine, but in fullscreen or even maximized window, the cursor movement is choppy. I noticed that disabling pro motion dysplay mode and setting a strict screen frame rate surprisingly solves the problem. I think the lack of a true, strict 120Hz frequency on Macs, coupled with some dubious, behind-the-scenes dynamic frequency algorithms, is worth considering when addressing issues of this nature. I can't even conceptually imagine how to fix this or how to live with it, Godot should somehow let the system know that Pro Motion shouldn't use frequency reduction to save battery.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5435116806/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]